            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-36054-krb5-multidev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-36054 medium vulnerability for krb5-multidev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "lib/kadm5/kadm_rpc_xdr.c in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) before 1.20.2 and 1.21.x before 1.21.1 frees an uninitialized pointer. A remote authenticated user can trigger a kadmind crash. This occurs because _xdr_kadm5_principal_ent_rec does not validate the relationship between n_key_data and the key_data array count."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-36054\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: krb5-multidev\nVersion: 1.17-3+deb10u5\nFix Version: 1.17-3+deb10u6\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-36054](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-36054)",
