            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-46218-libcurl4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-46218 medium vulnerability for libcurl4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "This flaw allows a malicious HTTP server to set \"super cookies\" in curl that are then passed back to more origins than what is otherwise allowed or possible. This allows a site to set cookies that then would get sent to different and unrelated sites and domains.  It could do this by exploiting a mixed case flaw in curl's function that verifies a given cookie domain against the Public Suffix List (PSL). For example a cookie could be set with `domain=co.UK` when the URL used a lower case hostname `curl.co.uk`, even though `co.uk` is listed as a PSL domain."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-46218\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libcurl4\nVersion: 7.64.0-4+deb10u6\nFix Version: 7.64.0-4+deb10u8\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-46218](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-46218)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-46218**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl4  | 7.64.0-4+deb10u6  | 7.64.0-4+deb10u8  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2023-46218](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-46218)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
