            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-39615-libxml2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-39615 medium vulnerability for libxml2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Xmlsoft Libxml2 v2.11.0 was discovered to contain an out-of-bounds read via the xmlSAX2StartElement() function at /libxml2/SAX2.c. This vulnerability allows attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via supplying a crafted XML file. NOTE: the vendor's position is that the product does not support the legacy SAX1 interface with custom callbacks; there is a crash even without crafted input."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-39615\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libxml2\nVersion: 2.9.4+dfsg1-7+deb10u6\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-39615](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-39615)",
